__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Per-machine Claude Code permissions, and its backups
.claude/

# Generated documentation manual — rebuild with `python docs/build_html.py`.
# Committing it would be a second copy of every claim in docs/, which is the duplication
# that folder exists to avoid: a committed page goes stale the moment the markdown changes
# without a rebuild, which is precisely the failure the docs themselves keep hitting.
#
# The builder now emits six pages rather than one, and caches rendered mermaid SVG. Both are
# generated from markdown in this tree, so both are that same second copy.
docs/index.html
docs/overview.html
docs/features.html
docs/guides.html
docs/architecture.html
docs/reference.html
docs/_mermaid_cache/

# The executive brief, same reasoning: its content lives in `docs/build_exec_brief.py` (the
# FEATURES table), so the rendered page and the PDF are a second copy of that -- and they carry
# readiness claims, which are the claims most likely to be quoted after they stop being true.
# Rebuild with `python docs/build_exec_brief.py`; the generator and the diagrams it uses are
# both committed, so anyone cloning this repo can produce the PDF.
docs/EXECUTIVE_BRIEF.html
docs/EXECUTIVE_BRIEF.pdf
docs/EXECUTIVE_BRIEF.__probe.html
